<main>
    <section class="vb-hero fade-up fade-up-2">
        <div class="vb-left">
            <h1>A shared knowledge graph for you and your AI</h1>
            <p class="tagline">Parachute Vault is a self-hosted memory layer that connects every AI you use. Notes, tags, links, project context — one graph, on your machine, over MCP.</p>

            <p class="vb-problem-label">Why it exists</p>
            <ul class="vb-problem-list">
                <li>Claude Code, Claude Chat, ChatGPT, Gemini — each starts from scratch, siloed from the others</li>
                <li>Your memory is one flat pile instead of organized by project and context</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="vb-right">
            <p class="vb-install-label">Get started</p>
            <div class="code-inline">
                <code>bun add -g @openparachute/cli &amp;&amp; parachute install vault</code>
            </div>
            <p class="vb-install-note">Requires <a href="https://bun.sh" target="_blank">Bun</a>. Run inside any Claude Code session — Vault is picked up automatically. <a href="/install/">Full install guide &rarr;</a></p>
            <a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute-vault" class="vb-cta-btn" target="_blank">View on GitHub</a>
            <a href="/blog/" class="vb-gh-link">Read the launch post &rarr;</a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="vb-body fade-up fade-up-3">
        <div class="vb-body-section">
            <h2>How it connects your AIs</h2>
            <p>Run <code>parachute expose tailnet</code> and your Vault is reachable over HTTPS on your Tailscale network. Point Claude Desktop, ChatGPT Desktop, Gemini, or any MCP-compatible tool at the same URL.</p>
            <p>Notes written in one session appear in the next. Project context follows you across tools, not just sessions.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="vb-body-section">
            <h2>The graph compounds over time</h2>
            <p>Wikilinks resolve, tags accrete, notes point at each other. As your AIs read and write, context gets richer — organized by project, linked by topic, queryable as a whole.</p>
            <p>Everything is a SQLite file on your disk. Your data is yours, portable, and doesn't require us to exist.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="vb-principles fade-up fade-up-4">
        <h2>Principles</h2>
        <div class="vb-principles-grid">
            <div class="vb-principle">
                <strong>Local-first</strong>
                <span>SQLite on your disk. Nothing in the cloud unless you ask.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="vb-principle">
                <strong>Open standard</strong>
                <span>Built on MCP. Any AI today or next year.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="vb-principle">
                <strong>Open source</strong>
                <span>AGPL. Read every line of code that touches your notes.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="vb-principle">
                <strong>Extensible</strong>
                <span>Small, stable service contracts. Plug in your own modules.</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</main>
